# Wire-format FRAME snapshot — DO NOT edit by hand.
# File: snapshots/wire_frames.snap
# Each entry is a full Rynk frame — a 3-byte header (CMD u16 LE + SEQ u8) + postcard
# payload, COBS-encoded with a trailing 0x00 delimiter — one per protocol message; the
# label names the decoded payload (`()` = empty). A diff means the header, a CMD number,
# or a message frame changed. If intentional, bump ProtocolVersion::CURRENT and regenerate:
#   UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 cargo test -p rmk-types --features host wire_frames
# Format: <label>  <hex bytes>

